
@{
    ViewBag.Title = "_Terms";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<div class="rbt-overlay-page-wrapper privacy-page terms-page">

    <div class="breadcrumb-image-container breadcrumb-style-max-width">
        <div class="breadcrumb-image-wrapper">
            <div class="breadcrumb-dark"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="breadcrumb-content-top text-center">
            <h1 class="title">Terms and Conditions</h1>
            <p class="mb--20">Certainly! Below is a tailored Terms and Conditions page for CoursesHub, focused on students enrolling in Training Provider programs via your platform in compliance with Australian law</p>
            <ul class="page-list">
                <li class="rbt-breadcrumb-item"><a href="@Url.Action("Index","Index")">Home</a></li>
                <li>
                    <div class="icon-right"><i class="feather-chevron-right"></i></div>
                </li>
                <li class="rbt-breadcrumb-item active">Terms and Conditions</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>


    <div class="rbt-putchase-guide-area breadcrumb-style-max-width rbt-section-gapBottom">
        <div class="rbt-article-content-wrapper">
            <div class="post-thumbnail mb--30 position-relative text-center">
                <img src="~/assets/images/blog/terms-animated.svg" alt="CoursesHub terms and conditions - know your rights and responsibilities">
            </div>
            <div class="content">
                <h4>Acceptance of Terms</h4>
                <p>
                    By accessing, using, or enrolling in Training Provider courses via CoursesHub, you agree to be bound by these Terms and all applicable laws and regulations. If you do not accept these Terms, do not use our website or services.
                </p>

                <h4>Services Provided by CoursesHub</h4>
                <p>
                    CoursesHub is an online platform that connects students with universities and academic programs. We provide information about various Training Provider courses, allow students to explore and compare options, and facilitate the application process. Our services include:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Training Provider course listings across a wide range of disciplines.</li>
                        <li>The ability to submit applications to selected universities.</li>
                        <li>Access to detailed information regarding universities, entry requirements, deadlines, and tuition fees.</li>
                        <li>Support and guidance throughout the application and enrollment process.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>

                <h4>Account Registration and Security</h4>
                <p>
                    To access certain features on our platform, you may be required to create an account. You must provide accurate and complete information during registration and keep your account details up-to-date. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account and password and agree to notify us immediately of any unauthorized use of your account.
                </p>

                <h4>Use of the Platform</h4>
                <p>
                    You agree to use CoursesHub solely for lawful purposes and in accordance with these Terms. You will not:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Submit false or misleading information.</li>
                        <li>Use the platform to engage in any unlawful activities.</li>
                        <li>Attempt to bypass any security features or access restricted areas of the platform.</li>
                        <li>Distribute any content that may violate intellectual property rights or harm others.</li>
                    </ul>
                    CoursesHub reserves the right to suspend or terminate your account if we believe you have violated these Terms.
                </p>

                <h4>Application and Enrollment Process</h4>
                <p>
                    CoursesHub provides a simplified process for students to apply to universities. However, it is your responsibility to ensure that the information provided in your application is complete and accurate. By submitting an application through CoursesHub, you agree to:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Ensure all documents, including transcripts, identification, and other required materials, are submitted in a timely manner.</li>
                        <li>Comply with the Training Provider’s entry requirements, deadlines, and admission procedures.</li>
                        <li>Understand that CoursesHub is not responsible for the acceptance or rejection of applications by universities.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>

                <h4>Fees and Payment</h4>
                <p>
                    CoursesHub may charge fees for certain services, such as application processing or Training Provider consultation. Any fees will be clearly outlined at the point of transaction. Fees for university courses are determined by the individual institutions and are separate from any fees charged by CoursesHub.
                    All transactions made through the CoursesHub platform will be processed securely. Payments for CoursesHub services are non-refundable unless specified otherwise.
                </p>

                <h4>Intellectual Property</h4>
                <p>
                    The content on the CoursesHub website, including but not limited to text, images, logos, graphics, course listings, and design, is protected by intellectual property laws. You may not reproduce, distribute, or create derivative works of any content without prior written consent from CoursesHub.
                </p>

                <h4>Privacy and Data Protection</h4>
                <p>
                    Your use of the CoursesHub platform is also governed by our Privacy Policy, which explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information. By using our platform, you consent to our collection and use of your data in accordance with the Privacy Policy.
                </p>

                <h4>Limitation of Liability</h4>
                <p>
                    CoursesHub makes every effort to provide accurate and up-to-date information, but we do not guarantee the accuracy, completeness, or reliability of the content provided on the platform.
                </p>
                <p>
                    To the fullest extent permitted by law, CoursesHub is not liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from the use of our platform or services. This includes, but is not limited to, any issues related to application submissions, Training Provider acceptance, or enrollment.
                </p>

                <h4>Dispute Resolution</h4>
                <p>
                    In the event of a dispute, we encourage you to contact us at [support@courseshub.com] to resolve the issue. If the dispute cannot be resolved through direct communication, you agree to use alternative dispute resolution methods. Disputes that cannot be resolved via these methods will be handled in the courts of [Your State or Territory], Australia.
                </p>

                <h4>Refund Policy</h4>
                <p>
                    Fees for CoursesHub services are non-refundable except where specified by Australian Consumer Law. For any course or Training Provider-related payments, you must refer to the refund policies provided by the individual universities.
                </p>
                <p>
                    If you are dissatisfied with our services, please contact us to discuss your concerns. We strive to ensure that all our students have a smooth and positive experience.
                </p>

                <h4>Modifications to Terms</h4>
                <p>
                    CoursesHub reserves the right to modify or update these Terms at any time. Any changes will be posted on this page with the updated date at the top. It is your responsibility to review these Terms periodically to stay informed of any changes.
                </p>
                <p>
                    By continuing to use CoursesHub after any modifications are posted, you agree to comply with the revised Terms.
                </p>

                <h4>Governing Law</h4>
                <p>
                    These Terms are governed by the laws of Australia and are subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of [Your State or Territory], Australia.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@section scripts{
    <script src="@CoursesHub.AssetVersion.Url("~/assets/js/main.js")"></script>
}